{"timestamp": 1783626183.036532, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 27, "data": {"caller": "player_4", "reason": "Eve reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "lower_engine", "victim_name": "Diana"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1783626183.037579, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 27, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1783626191.3421671, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 27, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I reported Diana\u2019s body in lower_engine. My route this round was cafeteria \u2192 medbay \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 oxygen \u2192 upper_engine \u2192 lower_engine. \n\nI saw Alice at security around tick 8, then electrical around tick 12, and later in upper_engine around tick 25. I saw Bob in electrical around tick 10. I didn\u2019t see Diana alive this round, and when I got to lower_engine her body was there.\n\nSince Alice was in upper_engine shortly before I found the body in lower_engine, she was the closest person I saw to the body location. Bob I only saw earlier in electrical, so I can\u2019t place him near the body from my own vision."}}
{"timestamp": 1783626207.828445, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 27, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Eve, that leaves out the key thing I saw: I was in lower_engine before going up, and Diana was alive there at ticks 20, 21, and 22. Bob entered lower_engine from storage at tick 22 while Diana was still there.\n\nAfter that I went to upper_engine. Eve came into upper_engine from oxygen at tick 24, then left toward lower_engine at tick 25 and reported the body. I did not go back down to lower_engine after leaving.\n\nSo from my perspective, Bob was the last person I saw physically in lower_engine with Diana alive. Eve could technically be self-reporting, but the timing points much more strongly to Bob having the opportunity. Bob needs to explain what happened in lower_engine after tick 22, because right now I\u2019m leaning Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1783626228.50744, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 27, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I get why that looks bad from Alice\u2019s angle, but I did not stay in lower_engine. My route was weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage \u2192 lower_engine, then I doubled back to storage. When I came in around tick 22, I saw Diana there and I also saw Alice leaving lower_engine toward upper_engine. I didn\u2019t hang around with Diana after that.\n\nThe part that worries me is Alice is saying \u201cBob was last with Diana,\u201d but from my view Alice was literally in lower_engine with Diana right before I arrived and left immediately as I came in. Then Eve says she found the body after coming down from upper_engine. So the possible windows are not just me \u2014 it\u2019s Alice leaving that room right at the timing, or Eve self-reporting after going down.\n\nI\u2019m not claiming Eve is definitely bad because reporting makes sense if she found it, but Alice framing it like I was alone there for a long time is not accurate. I was passing through and went back storage. Alice was the one already there with Diana."}}
{"timestamp": 1783626248.979912, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 27, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I\u2019m going to be clear: Alice and Bob both place Diana alive in lower_engine when Bob enters around tick 22. Alice then goes up, and I saw Alice in upper_engine at tick 25 right before I went down and reported.\n\nBob\u2019s defense is that Alice was there earlier, but if Bob is admitting Diana was alive when he arrived and Alice was leaving, then that actually clears Alice more than it accuses her. The only person left with direct opportunity after Diana was last seen alive is Bob, unless you think I self-reported, but I came straight from upper_engine and reported immediately.\n\nWith three of us left, I don\u2019t think we can skip. I think this is Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1783626265.5713222, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 27, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Bob, I hear you saying you \u201cjust passed through,\u201d but that\u2019s the whole problem: Diana was alive in lower_engine at tick 22 when you entered from storage, and after that I left to upper_engine. I saw Eve come into upper_engine from oxygen at tick 24, then go down and report right away at tick 25.\n\nSo the timeline is basically:\n- Diana alive in lower_engine.\n- Bob enters lower_engine with Diana there.\n- I leave upward.\n- Eve is seen in upper_engine coming from oxygen, then reports lower_engine immediately after going down.\n\nIf Eve were the Duck, she would\u2019ve had to go down, kill, and report instantly instead of just taking the win by killing at 3. That makes way less sense to me than Bob killing after I left and then claiming he doubled back with no witness.\n\nI\u2019m still voting Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1783626284.4757278, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 27, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "The thing I\u2019m not okay with is how cleanly Alice and Eve are trying to make this sound when there are holes.\n\nEve, your route doesn\u2019t include electrical, but you said you saw me in electrical around tick 10. I also saw you there. So why did you leave that out? That matters because now your \u201cstraight route\u201d is being used to make you look cleared.\n\nAnd Alice, you keep saying I was \u201cleft with Diana,\u201d but from my view you were already in lower_engine with Diana and left right as I came in. I passed through and doubled back to storage \u2014 I did not sit there with her. The only people making this a locked Bob vote are the two people whose stories conveniently clear each other.\n\nAt 3, a coordinated wrong vote loses. I\u2019m voting Eve here because the report timing plus the omitted electrical stop feels like a self-report frame."}}
